Based on LitMatrix 1.1.0 by bapungiri:
https://github.com/bapungiri/litmatrix
Tag v1.1.0, commit f56af00d742a217d08492df14ea572ac9ddc9b45.

The bootstrap lifecycle, native DOM construction, note-section editing,
and annotation navigation patterns are adapted from LitMatrix. The icon
is copied from LitMatrix. The project identity, scoped repository, stable
field codec, Chinese UI, CSV exporter, packaging and tests are modifications
made on 2026-11-02. The original LitMatrix installation is not modified.

Renamed from Project LitMatrix to ResearchGrid on 2026-11-02.
The legacy add-on ID and data identifiers remain unchanged for upgrades.

This work is licensed under GNU AGPL version 3 or (at your option) any later
version. See LICENSE. Corresponding source is supplied in the adjacent
research-grid-0.9.3-source.zip and in this project directory.
There is no automatic update endpoint. AI API requests are sent only when explicitly initiated by the user, to the user-configured endpoint.

CSV/TSV blank templates, parsing, identity matching, import preview and
transactional multi-paper import were added on 2026-11-03.

Objective-fact extraction prompts and selectable per-field summary detail
were added on 2026-11-03.

Sequential multi-paper AI drafts and persistent project-scoped text
highlights were added on 2026-11-04.

Double-click text editing and direct reading-mode highlighting replaced
the editor highlight-preview workflow on 2026-11-04.

Per-project tag visibility and selectable read-only Zotero metadata columns,
with ordered CSV export, were added on 2026-11-04.

Searchable collection trees and per-project multi-selection overview with
project-qualified edit, highlight and AI routing were added on 2026-11-04.

Per-project resizable columns and a native DOM/SVG project mind map with
draggable branches and persistent local layouts were added on 2026-11-04.
The mind-map interactions were informed by Better Notes (windingwind),
https://github.com/windingwind/zotero-better-notes . Its GoJS distribution
and source code are not included in this plugin.

Highlight saving now patches the affected cell and retains reading offsets
during background Zotero refreshes (2026-11-04).

Compact toolbar disclosures and optional field guidance in smaller table
headers were added on 2026-11-04.

Project navigation now locates the corresponding table section while
preserving horizontal reading position (2026-11-04).
